WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.462 --> 00:00:03.212
[music]

2
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:09.243
[Instructor] You know, if you take
the word Unity and add an R sound,

3
00:00:09.243 --> 00:00:13.060
you get Unitry, which kind
of sounds like unit three.

4
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:17.686
It's a pretty amazing coincidence,
because we are about to start Unit 3.

5
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:22.050
In this Unit, we will create
a beautiful, fast-paced,

6
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.080
endless side-scrolling game

7
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.596
where the player needs to jump
over obstacles in their path.

8
00:00:27.596 --> 00:00:31.510
[music] [game sounds]
[explosion]

9
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.351
Now, as you were watching
and listening to that,

10
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.330
you probably noticed
that it felt a lot more polished

11
00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.424
than either of our previous prototypes.

12
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.890
That's because it had Animation,
Sound,

13
00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.900
and Particle Effects.

14
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.280
Did you see the character
running, jumping,

15
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.380
and dramatically falling over?

16
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.404
Did you hear the Sound Effects
and Music in the background?

17
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.522
Did you see the little Particle
Effects kicking up from the back

18
00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:59.206
of the character's feet and the massive
explosion at the end? [explosion]

19
00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.849
It's these little touches
that will take your good Project

20
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.980
and make it great. These elements
help immerse the player

21
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.000
in the environment you've created.

22
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.350
Being able to add them
to your Projects

23
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.369
will be a literal game changer.

24
00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.139
So let's start creating.

25
00:01:16.139 --> 00:01:18.159
[music]
